  "body": "### Summary\n\nFollow-up to #308 / PR #315. Two cases need fixing:\n- A `PostingForm` loaded before an account switch in the same `HFRSession` still carries the old page's `hash_check` and `pseudo`.\n- A `PostingForm` loaded before a logout has the same problem.\n\nSubmitting such a form sends it through the new cookies. HFR refuses it with the bad-token answer (`W17b`), so nothing crosses accounts, but the user sees HFR's refusal instead of a clear local error.\n\n### Scope\n- Keep the `HashCheckSeed` taken by `PostingFlow.loadForm` in `PostingForm` (`Packages/HFRKit/Sources/HFRClient/Posting/PostingForm.swift:29`).\n- `submit` refuses locally, before any request, when the session no longer matches the seed's identity (`userKey`). It returns a typed error, for example `sessionChanged`.\n- Optional nits from the same review, if this PR already touches these files:\n  - `Posting/HashCheckSeed.swift:4` duplicates the concept of `Session/RefreshUpdate.swift:6` (`RefreshSeed`). Move it to `Session/` or cross-reference the two.\n  - The doc comment of `Tests/HFRClientTests/Support/ScriptedFlagSession.swift:6` still says \"A flag session\". The two scripted sessions also share the same login-adoption code.\n\n### Sources\n- The Fable review on #315 (finding 1, low).\n- PR #315, section \"Out of scope\".\n- The app uses one `HFRSession` per account (`AccountsModel`), so this needs a re-login with other credentials into the same session, or a logout. That makes this low priority.\n\n### Acceptance criteria\n- A test loads a form, adopts a login of another account (or a logout) in the session, then submits. It expects the local error and no POST.\n- A same-account re-login does not trigger the local refusal. The refreshed token is HFR's to judge, as in #315.\n- `swift test` passes; SwiftLint passes.",
